# Files that run inside a Linux container or on a Linux host must keep Unix line endings on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says:
# a shell script with CRLF fails with "bad interpreter", a CRLF Caddyfile or compose file is read differently, and the compose file is
# also matched line by line by a test (e2e/server-boundaries.spec.ts).
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
deploy/** text eol=lf
*.caddy text eol=lf
Caddyfile* text eol=lf
.env.production.example text eol=lf
